    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "A design student drew Nike's Swoosh, and got $35 for it.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 2.63,
        "window": 3.23,
        "fill": 0.814
      },
      {
        "scene": "student",
        "text": "She was paid by the hour. And the man who paid her didn't even love it.",
        "start": 3.53,
        "seconds": 2.85,
        "window": 3.5,
        "fill": 0.814
      },
      {
        "scene": "who",
        "text": "Phil Knight, an accounting teacher at Portland State, sold running shoes on the side. In 1971 he needed a logo, fast, and asked a design student, Carolyn Davidson.",
        "start": 7.03,
        "seconds": 8.09,
        "window": 8.53,
        "fill": 0.948
      },
      {
        "scene": "wing",
        "text": "So why did Nike keep a logo its boss didn't love? There was no time left, and the shoes had to ship.",
        "start": 15.57,
        "seconds": 4.35,
        "window": 5.0,
        "fill": 0.87
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "Did she ever get more? Twelve years later, Knight thanked her: a gold Swoosh ring, and 500 Nike shares.",
        "start": 20.57,
        "seconds": 4.32,
        "window": 5.0,
        "fill": 0.864
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "Last year, Nike sold $46.4B of shoes and clothes, most of it under the Nike name.",
        "start": 25.57,
        "seconds": 4.56,
        "window": 5.2,
        "fill": 0.877
      },
      {
        "scene": "ending",
        "text": "Ring, or the shares: which thank-you would you take? Look down. That Swoosh cost $35.",
        "start": 30.77,
        "seconds": 4.31,
        "window": 4.97,
        "fill": 0.867
      }
    ]
